{"status":"ok","message-type":"work-list","message-version":"1.0.0","message":{"facets":{},"total-results":1960749,"items":[{"indexed":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,26]],"date-time":"2025-11-26T14:05:32Z","timestamp":1764165932394,"version":"3.46.0"},"posted":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,10]]},"group-title":"PsyArXiv","reference-count":0,"publisher":"Center for Open Science","license":[{"start":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,10]],"date-time":"2022-09-10T00:00:00Z","timestamp":1662768000000},"content-version":"unspecified","delay-in-days":0,"URL":"https:\/\/creativecommons.org\/licenses\/by\/4.0\/legalcode"}],"content-domain":{"domain":[],"crossmark-restriction":false},"abstract":"<p>Surveys frequently involve questions about factual events, such as \"Does the Earth go around the Sun, or does the Sun go around the Earth?\". From these surveys, we would like to say how many know the right answer to the question, and to what degree. Unfortunately, there is not much we can say, and it turns out we do not know how many Americans know Earth orbits the Sun.<\/p>","DOI":"10.31234\/osf.io\/wk4t9","type":"posted-content","created":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,11]],"date-time":"2022-09-11T01:01:09Z","timestamp":1662858069000},"source":"Crossref","is-referenced-by-count":0,"title":["How many Americans know Earth orbits the sun?"],"prefix":"10.31234","author":[{"ORCID":"https:\/\/orcid.org\/0000-0002-6876-6964","authenticated-orcid":true,"given":"Jonas","family":"Moss","sequence":"first","affiliation":[]}],"member":"15934","deposited":{"date-parts":[[2025,11,26]],"date-time":"2025-11-26T14:03:33Z","timestamp":1764165813000},"score":26.259449,"resource":{"primary":{"URL":"https:\/\/osf.io\/wk4t9_v1"}},"issued":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,10]]},"references-count":0,"URL":"https:\/\/doi.org\/10.31234\/osf.io\/wk4t9","published":{"date-parts":[[2022,9,10]]},"subtype":"preprint"}],"items-per-page":1,"query":{"start-index":0,"search-terms":null}}}